### Summary of Changes

#### 1. Code Changes
* Modified [packages/core/src/utils/errors.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_28052/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/core/src/utils/errors.ts#L36-L65):
  * Updated the `getErrorMessage` function so that any matched URL sequence (e.g. `https://antigravity.google.`) in the error message is correctly sanitized to strip trailing periods (e.g. `https://antigravity.google`). This keeps the URLs intact while removing invalid sentence-ending punctuation when formatting the interactive error report.

```typescript
  // Strip trailing periods from URLs in the error message.
  return message.replace(/https?:\/\/[^\s]+/g, (url) => {
    while (url.endsWith('.')) {
      url = url.slice(0, -1);
    }
    return url;
  });
```

#### 2. Unit Tests
* Updated [packages/core/src/utils/errors.test.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/small_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_28052/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/core/src/utils/errors.test.ts#L48-L57):
  * Added a concrete unit test in the `getErrorMessage` block verifying that trailing period URLs (e.g. `https://antigravity.google.`) are correctly sanitized to `https://antigravity.google`.

```typescript
  it('should sanitize error messages containing URLs with trailing periods', () => {
    expect(getErrorMessage(new Error('Failed to sign in. Please visit https://antigravity.google.')))
      .toBe('Failed to sign in. Please visit https://antigravity.google');
    expect(getErrorMessage('Please go to https://antigravity.google.'))
      .toBe('Please go to https://antigravity.google');
  });
```

